  "accepted_results": [
    "Conditional true-cardinality transfer and universal all-q folding; N5 consecutive obstruction to adaptive worst-case endpoint supply.",
    "N4 (0,1,3,4) refutes direct small-reciprocal OR adaptive packet supply; existing bounded-height theorem handles the tuple.",
    "Exact rounding displacement is norm(beta*tau)/p. Free-time E_r is equivalent to original integer chosen-runner witness. Retained own-margin S_r is distinct and universally false at N4 consecutive by an exact endpoint identity.",
    "One supplied Kumar proof version fails strict boundary and independent finite nesting controls; no broader literature conclusion."
  ],
  "qualifications": [
    "Only distinct adjacent ratio values guarantee nonvanishing; accepted packet theorems explicitly require nowhere-zero collision.",
    "Packet failures do not refute LRC, a union with existing height/insertion methods, or a restriction to legitimate minimal counterexamples.",
    "Pair-sum completeness and new affine results are reviewed manuscript arguments, not newly kernel checked."
  ],
